I think there’s a genuinely interesting idea here! 🎮🪙 You’re imagining a system where each game has its own token, people can buy that token to participate in the game’s economy, and the creators can benefit when their game becomes more popular.

That could become an innovative part of Freedom World. But I would make one important distinction before we build it: buying a game and buying a token connected to a game aren’t necessarily the same thing.

Let me show you how I would approach this.

🌎 Freedom World: Game Token Economy

🪙 1. Give each game its own economic model

Imagine we release Freedom World: The Portal Awakens.

The development team creates an amazing game. Players love the characters, explore the mazes, and want to support the creators.

We could give them three ways to participate.

Option A: Buy the game

A player pays a normal purchase price and receives access to the game.

For example:

* Game price: $20.
* The player receives the agreed game license.
* The creator team receives its contractual share.
* Freedom World receives its agreed platform share.

This is the simplest model for players to understand.

Option B: Buy the game’s token

A player purchases a token associated with the game.

Depending on its design, the token could provide specific benefits, such as:

* Access to optional game features.
* Special cosmetic items.
* Participation in certain community activities.
* Access to a creator-supported marketplace.

The exact rights would be established before launch.

However, owning a game token wouldn’t automatically mean owning a copy of the game, unless the token’s terms explicitly provide a game license or access right.

We would also need to determine whether the token could be transferred, traded, or redeemed, and whether doing so creates additional legal obligations.

Option C: A game with both purchases and a token economy

This is the model I would investigate first.

Players could purchase the game normally, while the token supports optional features of its economy.

That way, someone who simply wants to play doesn’t have to understand cryptocurrency. People who want the additional token functionality can choose to participate.

The game remains playable and valuable without requiring players to speculate on a token.

